WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 12 Student Video
Unit 3, Lesson 4: Designer

1
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.670
Imagine you go hiking in a desert canyon.

2
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.710
You see some rocks, some cacti, maybe some caves in the canyon sides.

3
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:33.190
What would you conclude is the best explanation for the features you saw before you?

4
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:39.550
Well, obviously you think that natural forces, wind, erosion, maybe water, were at

5
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:39.790
work.

6
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:46.010
But what if you went hiking into a desert canyon and this time carved into the walls

7
00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:51.410
was an ancient city? Now, what would you conclude is the best

8
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:52.310
explanation?

9
00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.030
There actually is a place like this.

10
00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.650
It's the ancient city of Petra, which is found in the country of Jordan.

11
00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.190
Now, when modern day explorers came across Petra, do you think they stopped and

12
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.750
thought, oh my goodness, this is the result of natural forces?

13
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:13.930
Of course not. When you look at Petra today, you can see intricately carved pillars,

14
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.310
buildings into the side of the solid rock.

15
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.510
You can see tombs and even a complex tunnel system for water.

16
00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:28.850
So why do we recognize design in the city of Petra, but not in a typical canyon?

17
00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.290
Well, Petra has a feature that we call specified complexity.

18
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.330
It might sound complex or daunting, but it's actually common sense and intuitive

19
00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.850
when you think about it. If

20
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.030
something is specified, it has a particular pattern.

21
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.830
For example, take crystals.

22
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.790
Crystals are specified according to a certain pattern.

23
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.150
Shells are specified according to a pattern.

24
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.890
Even pulsars emit light at regular intervals.

25
00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:03.810
But nobody looks at these and assumes design because they lack complexity.

26
00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:09.430
They can easily be explained by the regular workings of the laws of nature.

27
00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:13.230
When something is complex, it has multiple parts.

28
00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.690
Take, for example, a pile of rocks.

29
00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.810
Any pile of rocks is actually quite complex.

30
00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:24.570
But we don't assume that a pile of rocks is designed because it lacks specified

31
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:30.170
complexity. So like a shell, like a crystal, like a pulsar that emits

32
00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.150
light, we don't assume that a pile of rocks was designed.

33
00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.050
Design requires both specificity and complexity.

34
00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.870
You see, natural forces alone can result in things being specified with a pattern,

35
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:49.450
such as we see in crystals. Or natural forces can bring about things to be complex,

36
00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:55.570
like a pile of rocks. But natural forces cannot create things with specified

37
00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:01.550
complexity, such as Petra. When we see something as intricate as

38
00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:07.370
an ancient city of Petra, we know that the best explanation is that it is the result

39
00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.490
of an intelligent designer.

40
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.890
This is how many scientific fields operate.

41
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.070
Take forensic science, for example.

42
00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:23.750
When a forensic scientist comes across a body, he or she asks two general questions.

43
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.450
Is it the result of natural causes, such as a heart attack?

44
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.270
Or is it the result of intelligent activity, homicide?

45
00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:37.230
And the forensic scientist will look for signs of specified complexity to come to

46
00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.970
the most reasonable explanation.

47
00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.610
Archaeologists do the same thing.

48
00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:47.050
When an archaeologist comes across some kind of ancient relic, he or she asks

49
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.910
themselves, is this the result of natural forces?

50
00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.130
Or is it the result

51
00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:55.770
of design? So they will look at the physical features of, say, a

52
00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:00.890
rock that they find. And if they find specified complexity, such as you would see on

53
00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.550
an arrowhead, then the archaeologist will conclude that the best explanation is that

54
00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.110
this is the result of intelligent design.

55
00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:14.550
And amazingly, we find the same patterns of design in nature itself.

56
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.790
Just take the human body. In the human body, in every single cell, we find DNA.

57
00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:25.950
And in DNA, as we have seen, we have both specificity and complexity.

58
00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:32.050
In fact, there is more information in DNA than in anything humans are close

59
00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:38.010
to creating. The best explanation for DNA is that it was designed by a creator

60
00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:43.110
of life. There are many other examples of design, such as we see in the Cambrian

61
00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:48.530
explosion, in irreducibly complex systems, and even in the origin of the universe

62
00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.570
itself.

63
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.440
This is why one of the most common objections against intelligent design fails.

64
00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:02.140
You maybe have heard people say well you're just making an argument from the gaps

65
00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:07.480
it's called the God of the gaps and the idea is we look at nature we don't have a

66
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.980
natural explanation and so we assume God.

67
00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.960
But that's not what we're doing we're not looking at nature saying well we lack an

68
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.140
explanation for DNA or we lack an explanation for fine-tuning therefore God did it.

69
00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.040
We're essentially saying two things we're saying number one nature can't explain it

70
00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:29.660
alone but we see the positive evidence of an intelligent agent we look at DNA

71
00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:34.660
we see specified complexity we look at the fine-tuning of the laws of physics we see

72
00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.800
specified complexity and as we have seen when we see that marker we know the best

73
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.540
explanation is that it is the result of an intelligent designer.

74
00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:49.960
Both naturalism and pantheism fail to adequately explain design in nature for

75
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.640
one basic reason they lack an intelligent agent a cosmic mind

76
00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.680
that can produce specified complexity.

77
00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:04.640
In fact they have to rely entirely upon chance time and the laws of nature

78
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:10.000
but this is like trying to rely upon wind erosion water and other natural

79
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.360
forces to explain the ancient city of Petra.

80
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:19.440
The most reasonable explanation for design in nature is that the world was actually

81
00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.280
designed. That's right design in nature points towards a

82
00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:30.720
designer. This of course should come as no surprise to those of us who believe in

83
00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:30.900
God.

84
00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:37.740
After all long before the discoveries of modern science the psalmist wrote that the

85
00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:43.040
heavens declare the glory of God the skies proclaim His Majesty.

86
00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.220
Day by day they spew forth speech night by night they display knowledge.

87
00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:54.360
In other words the psalmist knew that the natural world reveals truths about the

88
00:06:54.360 --> 00:07:00.040
Creator. If the world really is designed if the natural

89
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:05.580
world is actually filled with specified complexity then this raises a very

90
00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.180
important question. Who is this designer?

